### Verdict: SUPPORTED

### Justification
The fact-check confirms that Russia sent a plane carrying 60 tons of medical equipment—including ventilators, masks, and respirators—to the United States in April 2020, as reported by multiple sources ([NBC News](https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/russian-plane-coronavirus-medical-gear-lands-u-s-after-trump-n1174436), [Anadolu Agency](https://www.aa.com.tr/en/health/russia-sends-medical-aid-to-us-to-help-fight-covid-19/1788290)). U.S. officials acknowledged the shipment, which arrived in New York. Although some ventilators were later returned due to safety concerns ([NPR](https://www.npr.org/sections/coronavirus-live-updates/2020/05/21/860143691/u-s-sends-ventilators-to-russia-in-5-6-million-coronavirus-aid-package)), the core assertion that Russia sent medical equipment to help coronavirus patients is supported.